WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:04.610
House of the Dragon Episode 5 has a royal
wedding.

00:00:04.610 --> 00:00:09.139
So naturally, there’s politics, drama, and
a murder.

00:00:09.139 --> 00:00:11.049
What happens, and what does it mean?

00:00:11.049 --> 00:00:14.980
This video has no spoilers for Hot D beyond
Episode 5.

00:00:14.980 --> 00:00:20.700
The opening sequence is a symbolic family
tree showing the bloodline of House Targaryen.

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:23.519
And it’s slightly changed across episodes.

00:00:23.519 --> 00:00:29.390
The symbol for Alicent Hightower now has a
bloodline connecting to her husband King Viserys,

00:00:29.390 --> 00:00:33.940
and there are two bloodlines coming from her
– representing her son Aegon and her daughter

00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:34.940
Helaena.

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:41.050
The symbol for Rhaenyra now connects to Laenor
Velaryon, who she marries in this episode.

00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:46.460
In the previous episode, Viserys told Daemon
to go back to his wife in the Vale.

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:51.789
So now, in the Vale, we meet Daemon’s estranged
wife Rhea Royce.

00:00:51.789 --> 00:00:57.949
House Royce is famous for their ancient bronze
armour engraved with runes of the First Men.

00:00:57.949 --> 00:01:03.489
So Rhea’s clothes are decorated with runes
– which the show’s creators copied from

00:01:03.489 --> 00:01:04.670
Wikipedia.

00:01:04.670 --> 00:01:10.380
The Royce bronze armour, and their history
as Bronze Kings, is why Daemon calls Rhea

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:12.430
his “bronze bitch”.

00:01:12.430 --> 00:01:16.100
In Game of Thrones, House Royce is led by
Bronze Yohn Royce.

00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:21.930
He’s the father of Waymar Royce, who gets
killed by white walkers in Episode 1.

00:01:21.930 --> 00:01:27.030
The Royce castle is Runestone – just up
the coast from King’s Landing.

00:01:27.030 --> 00:01:29.550
So Daemon arrives and finds Rhea.

00:01:29.550 --> 00:01:34.350
And Rhea is immediately suspicious of him,
glancing over her shoulder.

00:01:34.350 --> 00:01:38.399
She insults Daemon, saying he should have
sex with a sheep.

00:01:38.399 --> 00:01:44.000
Cause previously, Daemon said that in the
Vale the sheep are prettier than the women.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:49.680
Rhea mocks Daemon, saying that Viserys rejected
Daemon by making Rhaenyra heir to the Throne

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:51.130
instead of him.

00:01:51.130 --> 00:01:55.899
And Rhea says that her marriage to Daemon
is still unconsummated – they’ve never

00:01:55.899 --> 00:01:57.250
had sex.

00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:58.880
Rhea says Daemon “couldn't finish”.

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:06.430
And we know Daemon has history of sexual dysfunction,
of not being able to have sex with Mysaria

00:02:06.430 --> 00:02:07.550
and Rhaenyra.

00:02:07.550 --> 00:02:14.010
So Rhea really knows how to hurt Daemon’s
insecurities about sex and family.

00:02:14.010 --> 00:02:19.380
She’s just as sharp-tongued as he is, so
it’s easy to see how Rhea and Daemon’s

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:22.600
personalities clashed, and the marriage failed.

00:02:22.600 --> 00:02:28.350
Daemon comes close, Rhea grabs her bow, her
horse rears up, Daemon touches it(?) and it

00:02:28.350 --> 00:02:32.080
falls, so that Rhea is crushed, paralysing
her.

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:37.750
Then Daemon kills her with a rock – to make
it look like she died by accident, falling

00:02:37.750 --> 00:02:39.220
off her horse.

00:02:39.220 --> 00:02:44.380
The books say that Rhea died in a “tragic
mishap”, falling and cracking her head on

00:02:44.380 --> 00:02:45.380
a rock.

00:02:45.380 --> 00:02:50.960
Daemon was on the Stepstones at the time,
so in the books Rhea’s death may have been

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:52.010
an accident.

00:02:52.010 --> 00:02:56.620
In the show, it is ambiguous whether Daemon
came here planning to kill Rhea, or if he

00:02:56.620 --> 00:03:00.920
just took the opportunity, but he kills his
hated wife.

00:03:00.920 --> 00:03:07.810
Which means Daemon is now free to remarry
whether for love, or for lust, or for power.

00:03:07.810 --> 00:03:11.020
Otto Hightower leaves King’s Landing.

00:03:11.020 --> 00:03:16.260
Viserys fired Otto as Hand of the King, because
Otto had manipulated Viserys, and undermined

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:20.210
Rhaenyra to try and make Otto’s grandson
Aegon heir to the Throne.

00:03:20.210 --> 00:03:26.020
Otto blames his daughter Alicent for getting
him fired, because Alicent sided with Rhaenyra,

00:03:26.020 --> 00:03:29.280
and said Rhaenyra was innocent of having sex
with Daemon.

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:32.250
But Otto says Rhaenyra is her enemy.

00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:38.260
Cause if Rhaenyra takes the Throne after Viserys
died, there’ll be “war” – many lords

00:03:38.260 --> 00:03:43.320
won’t accept a female ruler, and would prefer
Alicent’s son Aegon on the Throne.

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:48.730
Otto says Rhaenyra will need to kill Alicent’s
children, because they’re a threat to her

00:03:48.730 --> 00:03:49.730
claim.

00:03:49.730 --> 00:03:54.880
Otto says they must beat Rhaenyra and get
Aegon on the Throne.

00:03:54.880 --> 00:03:58.150
They must win the game of thrones, or die.

00:03:58.150 --> 00:04:03.980
Otto loves Alicent and wants to protect her,
but Alicent’s only in this dangerous situation

00:04:03.980 --> 00:04:08.870
because Otto pushed Alicent to marry Viserys,
and pushed for Aegon to be heir.

00:04:08.870 --> 00:04:14.750
Alicent went along with her family’s ambitions,
and now she and her children are in danger.

00:04:14.750 --> 00:04:21.510
Larys Strong, the Clubfoot, is the son of
Lyonel Strong, and the brother of Harwin Strong.

00:04:21.510 --> 00:04:27.520
Larys tells Alicent – subtly and indirectly
– that Maester Mellos gave Rhaenyra moon

00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:33.590
tea – hinting that Rhaenyra lied to Alicent,
and she really did have sex.

00:04:33.590 --> 00:04:39.280
Larys says Alicent can’t rely on Rhaenyra,
and that Larys will be Alicent’s ally.

00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:45.480
So Larys creates conflict, turning Alicent
against Rhaenyra, and positions himself up

00:04:45.480 --> 00:04:47.320
as a friend to the queen.

00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:53.060
It’s similar to how Littlefinger in Game
of Thrones creates chaos, to gain power.

00:04:53.060 --> 00:04:57.370
But how does Larys know about Rhaenyra’s
moon tea?

00:04:57.370 --> 00:05:02.500
Larys says that he’s just observant – we
saw him listening to the ladies at the hunt.

00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:06.920
But maybe he also has spies like Mysaria’s
little birds.

00:05:06.920 --> 00:05:10.360
Maybe he knows the secrets of the Red Keep
like Daemon.

00:05:10.360 --> 00:05:15.430
Maybe he’s working with the maesters – Larys’
dad Lyonel did study at the Citadel.

00:05:15.430 --> 00:05:18.860
Or maybe Larys’ knowledge is magical.

00:05:18.860 --> 00:05:24.310
YouTuber JoeMagician argues that Larys might
be a greenseer.

00:05:24.310 --> 00:05:29.910
Greenseers are people like Bran and Bloodraven
who use the magic of the old gods and the

00:05:29.910 --> 00:05:31.300
weirwood trees.

00:05:31.300 --> 00:05:36.350
Greenseers can see through the eyes of weirwoods,
and see through the eyes of animals, can see

00:05:36.350 --> 00:05:39.030
through time and space.

00:05:39.030 --> 00:05:44.010
Greenseers have the blood of the First Men,
the original humans in Westeros – that includes

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:50.180
House Stark like Bran, and House Blackwood
like Bloodraven, and House Strong like Larys

00:05:50.180 --> 00:05:53.430
– he also descends from First Men.

00:05:53.430 --> 00:05:59.000
Bloodraven says that greenseers have powerful
minds but are physically weak, just like Larys

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:01.280
is weak with his club foot.

00:06:01.280 --> 00:06:05.140
So it is plausible that Larys could be a greenseer.

00:06:05.140 --> 00:06:11.460
House Strong is based at Harrenhal, and Harrenhal
just happens to be right next door to the

00:06:11.460 --> 00:06:16.190
Isle of Faces, a mysterious island sacred
to the old gods.

00:06:16.190 --> 00:06:22.150
The isle has a grove of weirwood trees, watched
over by the mystical green men.

00:06:22.150 --> 00:06:27.060
Maybe the curious Larys Strong visited the
Isle of Faces, and learned magic from the

00:06:27.060 --> 00:06:28.380
green men.

00:06:28.380 --> 00:06:31.380
Maybe he can skinchange into animals.

00:06:31.380 --> 00:06:37.600
In the books, Bloodraven was once a spymaster
who skinchanged into crows to spy on people.

00:06:37.600 --> 00:06:44.330
In the books, Arya Stark also has this power,
and she skinchanges into a cat to spy on people.

00:06:44.330 --> 00:06:50.120
So maybe Larys skinchanges into these rats
we’ve seen in Hot D, using them to spy and

00:06:50.120 --> 00:06:53.980
listen to conversations in the Red Keep.

00:06:53.980 --> 00:06:58.020
And he could see through this weirwood to
witness all the important conversations that

00:06:58.020 --> 00:06:59.260
happen here.

00:06:59.260 --> 00:07:04.200
This scene with Alicent visually connects
Larys with the weirwood – at first it seems

00:07:04.200 --> 00:07:10.080
almost like Larys’ voice is coming from
the tree, like he’s watching through its

00:07:10.080 --> 00:07:11.240
eyes.

00:07:11.240 --> 00:07:13.419
For more on this theory, check out JoeMagician.

00:07:13.419 --> 00:07:17.510
But so far we don’t know for sure how Larys
knows what he knows.

00:07:17.510 --> 00:07:24.610
But he is a mysterious and powerful character,
and in a way he’s similar to Alicent.

00:07:24.610 --> 00:07:30.131
Cause Larys talks about a flower from Braavos
that isn’t native to King’s Landing, but

00:07:30.131 --> 00:07:32.260
still thrives here.

00:07:32.260 --> 00:07:37.510
Just like Larys and Alicent aren’t native
to the Red Keep, they aren’t royal Targaryens,

00:07:37.510 --> 00:07:40.940
but they may still thrive and grow strong
here.

00:07:40.940 --> 00:07:43.860
In the background, there’s an image of a
lemon tree.

00:07:43.860 --> 00:07:48.139
Which might be a subtle hint to a mystery
in the books.

00:07:48.139 --> 00:07:53.790
In the books, Daenerys remembers she once
lived in a house in Braavos with a lemon tree

00:07:53.790 --> 00:07:55.070
outside.

00:07:55.070 --> 00:07:59.830
Which is weird, because the books also say
that lemon trees don’t grow in Braavos,

00:07:59.830 --> 00:08:02.669
they only grow in warmer climates to the south.

00:08:02.669 --> 00:08:06.430
It’s not native – like Larys’ flower.

00:08:06.430 --> 00:08:11.750
Some fans speculate that Daenerys’ house
with the lemon tree was actually in Dorne

00:08:11.750 --> 00:08:14.090
for the Martell conspiracy.

00:08:14.090 --> 00:08:18.680
Viserys and Rhaenyra sail to Driftmark, the
island of House Velaryon.

00:08:18.680 --> 00:08:24.470
Viserys gets seasick and pukes, so his new
Hand of the King, Lyonel Strong, gives him

00:08:24.470 --> 00:08:26.850
a cloth to wipe the vomit.

00:08:26.850 --> 00:08:31.340
In Game of Thrones, Jaime says “The king
shits and the Hand wipes”.

00:08:31.340 --> 00:08:36.380
It’s the job of the Hand of the King to
solve the king’s problems and clean up his

00:08:36.380 --> 00:08:37.380
mess.

00:08:37.380 --> 00:08:42.010
It’s interesting that Viserys takes this
miserable boat journey instead of just flying

00:08:42.010 --> 00:08:43.090
a dragon.

00:08:43.090 --> 00:08:47.870
Viserys doesn’t have his own dragon anymore,
but he could’ve hitched a ride on Rhaenyra’s

00:08:47.870 --> 00:08:49.140
dragon Syrax.

00:08:49.140 --> 00:08:52.770
We’ve seen dragons used as passenger vehicles
before.

00:08:52.770 --> 00:08:55.840
Like they’re a big scaly flying minibus.

00:08:55.840 --> 00:09:01.980
Maybe Viserys is afraid to ride dragons, he
said they’re an uncontrollable dangerous

00:09:01.980 --> 00:09:02.980
power.

00:09:02.980 --> 00:09:06.580
They arrive at the Velaryon castle, High Tide.

00:09:06.580 --> 00:09:11.080
The Velaryons originally lived in a smaller
castle, but after Corlys made heaps of money

00:09:11.080 --> 00:09:15.090
on his voyages, he built this newer better
castle.

00:09:15.090 --> 00:09:20.250
High Tide is on its own small tidal island,
that’s only accessible by foot when the

00:09:20.250 --> 00:09:21.590
tide is low.

00:09:21.590 --> 00:09:26.330
Showing the Velaryon connection to sea power
and ships.

00:09:26.330 --> 00:09:30.760
Lyonel is offended that that the Velaryons
don’t greet King Viserys outside.

00:09:30.760 --> 00:09:35.089
It’s meant to be a big deal when the king
visits your home, like when King Robert visits

00:09:35.089 --> 00:09:37.200
the Starks in Game of Thrones.

00:09:37.200 --> 00:09:42.870
But Viserys is just greeted by Laena Velaryon,
the daughter of Corlys and Rhaenys.

00:09:42.870 --> 00:09:46.529
Previously, Viserys rejected Laena’s marriage
proposal.

00:09:46.529 --> 00:09:52.110
So now sending Laena to meet Viserys is a
reminder of how insulted Corlys felt that

00:09:52.110 --> 00:09:54.890
his family was a denied a royal marriage.

00:09:54.890 --> 00:10:00.420
Corlys meets Viserys inside, seated on his
Driftwood Throne.

00:10:00.420 --> 00:10:05.460
According to ancient legend, this Throne was
given to the Velaryons by the Merling King,

00:10:05.460 --> 00:10:07.900
a kind of mermaid sea god.

00:10:07.900 --> 00:10:14.839
It’s a total power move that Corlys has
the king come to him, and Corlys stands over

00:10:14.839 --> 00:10:15.839
Viserys.

00:10:15.839 --> 00:10:21.420
Corlys is a very proud man who wants everyone
to know how great he is.

00:10:21.420 --> 00:10:26.550
This room is called the Hall of Nine – it’s
full of treasures and trophies that Corlys

00:10:26.550 --> 00:10:28.800
got on his famous nine sea voyages.

00:10:28.800 --> 00:10:34.779
There’s a “snake orrery”, and a hanging
city, a giant sea shell.

00:10:34.779 --> 00:10:39.080
And now Corlys adds the Crabfeeder’s mask
to his collection.

00:10:39.080 --> 00:10:45.100
Corlys has achieved so much that he lives
in a museum of his own awesomeness, and yet

00:10:45.100 --> 00:10:48.040
Corlys is still not satisfied.

00:10:48.040 --> 00:10:54.680
Viserys proposes for his daughter and heir
Rhaenyra to marry Corlys’ son Laenor.

00:10:54.680 --> 00:10:59.250
He says this will finally unite the Targaryen
and Velaryons.

00:10:59.250 --> 00:11:05.490
Which is funny, cause Corlys Velaryon’s
wife Rhaenys Targaryen is standing right there.

00:11:05.490 --> 00:11:12.820
But Corlys is still angry that Rhaenys didn’t
inherit the Throne back at the Harrenhal Council.

00:11:12.820 --> 00:11:18.290
The marriage of Rhaenyra and Laenor is really
about making up for that rejection and finally

00:11:18.290 --> 00:11:21.250
marrying a Velaryon into the royal line.

00:11:21.250 --> 00:11:27.540
Corlys negotiates the details – like, traditionally,
children have their father’s family name.

00:11:27.540 --> 00:11:33.710
So will Rhaenyra and Laenor’s children,
the next rulers of Westeros, be called Velaryon?

00:11:33.710 --> 00:11:38.920
Viserys doesn’t want to the Targaryen royal
name to end with this marriage.

00:11:38.920 --> 00:11:44.100
So he says that Rhaenyra and Laenor’s children
will be called Velaryon, but when one inherits

00:11:44.100 --> 00:11:49.070
the Throne, they’ll be called Targaryen
to continue the Targaryen dynasty.

00:11:49.070 --> 00:11:54.400
So both Viserys and Corlys are very concerned
with their legacy and pride.

00:11:54.400 --> 00:11:59.190
Viserys may also be thinking of Aegon the
Conqueror’s dream, that a Targaryen will

00:11:59.190 --> 00:12:01.420
defeat the white walkers.

00:12:01.420 --> 00:12:07.529
But they agree to the marriage, forging a
stronger alliance between the last two Valyrian

00:12:07.529 --> 00:12:08.830
dragonriding families.

00:12:08.830 --> 00:12:12.600
Meanwhile, Rhaenyra and Laenor make their
own agreement.

00:12:12.600 --> 00:12:16.010
Laenor is gay – Joffrey Lonmouth is his
boyfriend.

00:12:16.010 --> 00:12:19.990
So marrying Rhaenyra is not what either of
them want.

00:12:19.990 --> 00:12:23.560
Corlys says that Laenor will grow out of being
gay.

00:12:23.560 --> 00:12:29.000
But Rhaenyra accepts Laenor’s sexuality
– she uses an analogy that some people like

00:12:29.000 --> 00:12:31.080
duck and some people like goose.

00:12:31.080 --> 00:12:35.360
This is based on a line in the books where
Mellos says it doesn’t matter that Laenor

00:12:35.360 --> 00:12:40.610
is gay, he should marry Rhaenyra anyway, because
Mellos doesn’t like fish, but when fish

00:12:40.610 --> 00:12:43.410
is served he’ll eat it anyway.

00:12:43.410 --> 00:12:47.640
Rhaenyra and Laenor agree that they’ll do
their duty, get married, make some babies,

00:12:47.640 --> 00:12:52.150
but on the side they’ll hook up with who
they want – Laenor can stay with Joffrey,

00:12:52.150 --> 00:12:55.600
and Rhaenyra can have Criston or whoever else
she wants.

00:12:55.600 --> 00:13:01.200
Rhaenyra must’ve been inspired earlier by
Daemon saying you can have sex outside your

00:13:01.200 --> 00:13:02.200
marriage.

00:13:02.200 --> 00:13:06.510
Rhaenyra and Laenor are both happy with this
compromise, but polyamorous relationships

00:13:06.510 --> 00:13:12.910
can cause drama especially if combined with
secrecy, politics and dragons.

00:13:12.910 --> 00:13:17.589
Rhaenys says this marriage puts her son Laenor
in danger.

00:13:17.589 --> 00:13:22.399
Like Otto, she says there will be conflict
between Rhaenyra and Aegon for the Throne.

00:13:22.399 --> 00:13:27.750
Corlys says he’s will to fight to put a
Velaryon’s child on the Throne.

00:13:27.750 --> 00:13:31.820
He says it’s justice, to make up for Rhaenys
not getting the Throne.

00:13:31.820 --> 00:13:38.589
But Rhaenys she’s over that, she cares more
about her family’s safety than she cares

00:13:38.589 --> 00:13:39.820
for the Throne.

00:13:39.820 --> 00:13:45.930
She suggests Corlys is really motivated not
by justice, but by pride and power.

00:13:45.930 --> 00:13:53.160
Despite her fears, she’s dragged along with
Corlys’ ambitions, like Aemma with Viserys,

00:13:53.160 --> 00:13:55.540
and Alicent with Otto.

00:13:55.540 --> 00:14:02.670
Criston feels guilty and ashamed that he broke
his Kingsguard oath by having sex with Rhaenyra.

00:14:02.670 --> 00:14:06.260
So Criston asks Rhaenyra to run away with
him to the east.

00:14:06.260 --> 00:14:12.930
To escape their responsibilities as Kingsguard
and princess, and to be free and married together.

00:14:12.930 --> 00:14:17.899
Rhaenyra has said before that she wants to
escape her responsibilities and wants to travel

00:14:17.899 --> 00:14:18.899
the east.

00:14:18.899 --> 00:14:22.250
But lately, Rhaenyra has accepted her political
duties.

00:14:22.250 --> 00:14:27.330
Viserys told her about Aegon the Conqueror’s
dream that the Targaryen dynasty must protect

00:14:27.330 --> 00:14:31.880
the world from the white walkers, and made
her promise to uphold this.

00:14:31.880 --> 00:14:34.730
So Rhaenyra says she’ll stay.

00:14:34.730 --> 00:14:39.000
Buut she could still keep Criston as a lover
on the side.

00:14:39.000 --> 00:14:43.500
Criston is insulted by this, he doesn’t
want to be a “whore”, used for sex.

00:14:43.500 --> 00:14:49.210
Which seems hypocritical – Criston expects
Rhaenyra to give up her crown and her family

00:14:49.210 --> 00:14:53.190
and her home, but Criston is too proud himself
to be a paramour?

00:14:53.190 --> 00:14:55.870
But it goes deeper.

00:14:55.870 --> 00:15:01.300
Because Criston’s whole identity, his greatest
achievement, is being a Kingsguard.

00:15:01.300 --> 00:15:05.860
He swore a sacred oath of chastity, to not
have sex.

00:15:05.860 --> 00:15:12.120
And he can’t live in that white cloak knowing
it’s a lie, knowing he could be killed for

00:15:12.120 --> 00:15:13.230
his crime.

00:15:13.230 --> 00:15:18.910
He sees running to the east as a way to escape
that shame, and marrying Rhaenyra as way to

00:15:18.910 --> 00:15:20.920
fix his sin.

00:15:20.920 --> 00:15:25.820
Running east is not a great idea, but it’s
the only idea he has.

00:15:25.820 --> 00:15:31.820
So when Rhaenyra says no, Criston loses his
one hope for a tolerable life.

00:15:31.820 --> 00:15:37.840
After speaking with Larys, Alicent suspects
that Rhaenyra lied, that maybe she did have

00:15:37.840 --> 00:15:39.490
sex with Daemon.

00:15:39.490 --> 00:15:45.950
So Alicent questions Rhaenyra’s guard Criston
– though, like Otto, Alicent is too proper

00:15:45.950 --> 00:15:51.110
and ashamed to directly say that she thinks
Rhaenyra and Daemon had sex.

00:15:51.110 --> 00:15:56.110
So Criston thinks Alicent is talking about
Rhaenyra having sex with him.

00:15:56.110 --> 00:16:03.149
Criston is so full of shame and fear, so desperate
for repentance that he confesses, and tells

00:16:03.149 --> 00:16:05.959
Alicent he had sex with Rhaenyra.

00:16:05.959 --> 00:16:10.180
He asks to be put to death, rather than gelded
or tortured.

00:16:10.180 --> 00:16:15.310
Cause when the Kingsguard Lucamore Strong
had sex, they cut off his penis and sent him

00:16:15.310 --> 00:16:16.329
to the Wall.

00:16:16.329 --> 00:16:22.540
And when the Kingsguard Terrence Toyne has
sex, the king has him cut to pieces slowly.

00:16:22.540 --> 00:16:25.460
Criston wants a quick honourable end.

00:16:25.460 --> 00:16:29.240
But Alicent doesn’t give him punishment
or absolution.

00:16:29.240 --> 00:16:35.970
She’s so stunned that she just lets him
go, leaving Criston to sink deeper into guilt

00:16:35.970 --> 00:16:40.930
and fear, knowing he could be killed for his
crime at any time.

00:16:40.930 --> 00:16:46.519
Alicent is angry not just that Rhaenyra lied
to her about not having sex, but also cause

00:16:46.519 --> 00:16:51.360
Alicent believing Rhaenyra is part of what
got her dad Otto fired.

00:16:51.360 --> 00:16:58.520
If she can’t trust Rhaenyra, and Otto is
gone, Alicent is more alone than ever.

00:16:58.520 --> 00:17:03.459
King Viserys is very sick from the infection
that started in his hand.

00:17:03.459 --> 00:17:10.329
Viserys’ actor said he’s now got something
like leprosy, deteriorating his body and bones.

00:17:10.329 --> 00:17:16.910
Which is partly a metaphor for his stress
and his failure as a king.

00:17:16.910 --> 00:17:19.549
Grand Maester Mellos treats Viserys with leeches.

00:17:19.549 --> 00:17:26.449
A new maester called Orwyle says a different
treatment might work better, but Mellos refuses..

00:17:26.449 --> 00:17:28.039
Which is suspicious.

00:17:28.039 --> 00:17:32.179
Mellos talks as though his treatments are
working, but they’re not..

00:17:32.179 --> 00:17:38.690
This started with a cut, and now the king’s
falling to pieces, yet Mellos refuses to try

00:17:38.690 --> 00:17:41.279
different treatments that might help.

00:17:41.279 --> 00:17:47.129
So some fans speculate that Mellos is deliberately
letting the king die, maybe in conspiracy

00:17:47.129 --> 00:17:49.470
with Otto and the Hightowers.

00:17:49.470 --> 00:17:54.739
They might hope that if Viserys is weak or
dead they can more easily get Aegon on the

00:17:54.739 --> 00:17:55.739
Throne.

00:17:55.739 --> 00:17:58.710
Viserys knows he might die soon.

00:17:58.710 --> 00:18:06.179
So he thinks on his legacy, and wonders if
he’d be remembered more if he had fought

00:18:06.179 --> 00:18:07.179
battles.

00:18:07.179 --> 00:18:13.160
His model city of Valyria is behind Viserys
– the empire of his ancestors is on his

00:18:13.160 --> 00:18:14.160
mind.

00:18:14.160 --> 00:18:19.840
But Lyonel says it’s a good thing that Viserys’
reign was peaceful – he continued the peaceful

00:18:19.840 --> 00:18:25.509
legacy of his grandfather King Jaehaerys.

00:18:25.509 --> 00:18:31.510
But Viserys has an ego, and knows that they
don’t sing songs for kings of peace.

00:18:31.510 --> 00:18:34.350
The Velaryons come to King’s Landing for
the wedding.

00:18:34.350 --> 00:18:40.320
And for the first time, we see Rhaenys’
dragon, called Meleys, “the Red Queen”.

00:18:40.320 --> 00:18:43.429
Meleys is a “magnificent scarlet she-dragon”.

00:18:43.429 --> 00:18:47.559
She was first ridden by Alyssa Targaryen,
the mother of Viserys and Daemon.

00:18:47.559 --> 00:18:52.609
And Meleys was once the fastest dragon in
Westeros.

00:18:52.609 --> 00:18:56.539
The other dragon here is Seasmoke, Laenor’s
dragon.

00:18:56.539 --> 00:19:01.220
Inside, Lord Jason Lannister arrives with
his twin brother Tyland.

00:19:01.220 --> 00:19:06.149
Jason makes a dumb women joke, and Rhaenyra
is not impressed.

00:19:06.149 --> 00:19:10.399
The Velaryons arrive in rich clothing showing
off their wealth.

00:19:10.399 --> 00:19:16.039
And then, just as Viserys is about to speak,
Daemon bloody Targaryen saunters in as though

00:19:16.039 --> 00:19:17.909
he owns the place.

00:19:17.909 --> 00:19:21.350
Just last episode, Viserys told Daemon to
never return.

00:19:21.350 --> 00:19:26.539
But now Viserys just lets Daemon return from
exile for the second time.

00:19:26.539 --> 00:19:32.159
Viserys seems incapable of saying no to his
family – and since his brother daughter

00:19:32.159 --> 00:19:37.480
and wife all want different things, this is
a recipe for conflict.

00:19:37.480 --> 00:19:42.899
When Viserys starts his speech, he’s interrupted
again by the arrival of Alicent in a brilliant

00:19:42.899 --> 00:19:44.470
green dress.

00:19:44.470 --> 00:19:51.230
Earlier, Alicent felt alone and betrayed,
so now she rises definitely and asserts her

00:19:51.230 --> 00:19:53.499
own power as queen.

00:19:53.499 --> 00:19:59.220
Green is a Hightower colour – Larys says
that the Hightower beacon burns green at times

00:19:59.220 --> 00:20:00.350
of war.

00:20:00.350 --> 00:20:05.210
So this is a rallying call for the Hightowers
to stand by her.

00:20:05.210 --> 00:20:12.320
Previously, Alicent wore red Targaryen clothes,
so now wearing green sets her apart from and

00:20:12.320 --> 00:20:14.580
against Rhaenyra.

00:20:14.580 --> 00:20:20.159
Previously, Rhaenyra called Alicent “sister”,
cause they were close like equals.

00:20:20.159 --> 00:20:26.979
But now, Alicent calls Rhaenyra “stepdaughter”,
setting herself above Rhaenyra.

00:20:26.979 --> 00:20:31.440
Green is a colour of envy – the director
said that Alicent had always been envious

00:20:31.440 --> 00:20:36.450
of Rhaenyra’s freedom while Alicent felt
trapped in her duty.

00:20:36.450 --> 00:20:42.999
Alicent has always been a proper lady – so
she shows her power not with swords or dragons,

00:20:42.999 --> 00:20:47.259
but with a dress, armouring herself in feminine
fashion.

00:20:47.259 --> 00:20:53.070
Her uncle, Lord Hobert Hightower, tells Alicent
that Oldtown stands with her.

00:20:53.070 --> 00:20:56.059
So the battle lines are being drawn.

00:20:56.059 --> 00:21:00.809
If there’s conflict for the Throne between
Alicent’s son Aegon and Rhaenyra, it looks

00:21:00.809 --> 00:21:05.899
like the Hightowers will support Aegon, while
the Velaryons will support Rhaenyra and Laenor.

00:21:05.899 --> 00:21:09.529
And all this tension is evident at the wedding.

00:21:09.529 --> 00:21:15.160
Rhaenyra and Laenor perform a dance that looks
like some.. dragon mating ritual with flapping

00:21:15.160 --> 00:21:18.999
wings – maybe this is an ancient Valyrian
dance.

00:21:18.999 --> 00:21:23.669
Rhaenyra’s actor said they called one of
these dance moves the “smelly fart”.

00:21:23.669 --> 00:21:26.669
Laenor says dancing is like combat.

00:21:26.669 --> 00:21:31.539
In the books, there’s a war called the Dance
of the Dragons – dancing being a metaphor

00:21:31.539 --> 00:21:35.299
for the deadly motion of politics and violence.

00:21:35.299 --> 00:21:40.850
So as the guests join the flowing movements
of this the dance, emotions and ambitions

00:21:40.850 --> 00:21:43.029
swirl amongst them.

00:21:43.029 --> 00:21:46.130
Daemon looks hungrily at Rhaenyra.

00:21:46.130 --> 00:21:48.149
Alicent glares in green.

00:21:48.149 --> 00:21:51.590
Criston boils with jealousy and shame.

00:21:51.590 --> 00:21:57.360
And there are closeups of meat being cut with
knives – foreshadowing bloody violence.

00:21:57.360 --> 00:22:02.490
According to interviews, this drummer is Mushroom
– Mushroom is the dwarf jester who tells

00:22:02.490 --> 00:22:06.870
tales of sex and murder in the book Fire &amp; Blood.

00:22:06.870 --> 00:22:12.249
Gerold Royce confronts Daemon, and accuses
him of murdering Rhea Royce.

00:22:12.249 --> 00:22:14.659
Daemon acts like he doesn’t care.

00:22:14.659 --> 00:22:20.519
And says that since Rhea was the heir to Runestone,
but Rhea had no kids, Daemon will claim the

00:22:20.519 --> 00:22:23.359
lordship of Runestone for himself.

00:22:23.359 --> 00:22:27.979
He says he’ll talk to the Lady of the Vale,
Jeyne Arryn, about it.

00:22:27.979 --> 00:22:33.350
And Gerold is shocked – maybe Gerold wants
to inherit Runestone himself, since he was

00:22:33.350 --> 00:22:34.379
Rhea’s cousin.

00:22:34.379 --> 00:22:40.059
So maybe Daemon’s implication here is that
if Gerold shuts up about Daemon killing Rhea,

00:22:40.059 --> 00:22:46.879
Daemon will let Gerold have Runestone – but
if Gerold pushes his accusation, Daemon will

00:22:46.879 --> 00:22:49.879
take Runestone to fuck with Gerold.

00:22:49.879 --> 00:22:56.130
And it seems to work – Gerold backs off.

00:22:56.130 --> 00:22:58.700
Daemon flirts with Laena Velaryon.

00:22:58.700 --> 00:23:04.519
Daemon seems helplessly attracted to women
with Valyrian blood and silver hair.

00:23:04.519 --> 00:23:10.889
Maybe because Valyrian women can birth Valyrian
children who can ride dragons – having dragonriders

00:23:10.889 --> 00:23:14.940
as children could be a way for Daemon to gain
power.

00:23:14.940 --> 00:23:19.840
Though last we heard, Laena was to be betrothed
to the son of the Sealord of Braavos, so she

00:23:19.840 --> 00:23:22.330
might not be single.

00:23:22.330 --> 00:23:28.590
After Laena, Daemon flirts with the next Valyrian
blonde, his niece, the bride, Rhaenyra.

00:23:28.590 --> 00:23:34.100
And Rhaenyra flirts back, saying sarcastically
but &gt;actually kind of for real though&lt; that

00:23:34.100 --> 00:23:37.159
Daemon should take her and marry her.

00:23:37.159 --> 00:23:43.070
Rhaenyra is still attracted to Daemon, and
has desires that Laenor won’t satisfy.

00:23:43.070 --> 00:23:48.220
Laenor’s boyfriend Joffrey figures out that
Criston is Rhaenyra’s secret lover – he

00:23:48.220 --> 00:23:51.330
can tell by how Criston watches Rhaenyra.

00:23:51.330 --> 00:23:55.529
So Joffrey tells Criston that he knows Criston’s
secret.

00:23:55.529 --> 00:24:00.260
He says that together they can protect both
their secret affairs – Joffrey’s affair

00:24:00.260 --> 00:24:03.249
with Laenor, and Criston’s with Rhaenyra.

00:24:03.249 --> 00:24:08.909
You can read this as a threat – like, Criston
better keep Joffrey and Laenor’s affair

00:24:08.909 --> 00:24:13.200
secret, or else Joffrey will expose Criston’s
secret affair.

00:24:13.200 --> 00:24:19.289
But while Joffrey is fairly relaxed about
these secrets, Criston is a ticking time bomb

00:24:19.289 --> 00:24:23.899
of pent up resentment, shame and suicidal
rage.

00:24:23.899 --> 00:24:30.149
Full of emotion, and scared that Joffrey will
blab his secret, Criston snaps, starts a fight,

00:24:30.149 --> 00:24:33.049
he punches Laenor, there’s chaos.

00:24:33.049 --> 00:24:36.960
So Lyonel sends his son Harwin in to get the
princess to safety.

00:24:36.960 --> 00:24:42.259
Harwin “Breakbones” is said to be the
strongest knight in Westeros, so if you need

00:24:42.259 --> 00:24:44.590
muscle, he’s your guy.

00:24:44.590 --> 00:24:50.989
In the fight, Criston’s emotions pour out
as he beats Joffrey to death.

00:24:50.989 --> 00:24:56.279
When we first met Criston, he seemed like
a fairytale noble white knight.

00:24:56.279 --> 00:25:01.950
But beneath that superficial appearance, Criston
is a brutal killer who makes his feelings

00:25:01.950 --> 00:25:05.639
and bad decisions everyone else’s problem.

00:25:05.639 --> 00:25:09.359
The show’s creators describe Criston as
a “thug”.

00:25:09.359 --> 00:25:13.330
And his violence was only made worse by his
knighthood.

00:25:13.330 --> 00:25:17.059
Knights are expected to defend their honour
with violence.

00:25:17.059 --> 00:25:22.479
A Kingsguard is taught that sex is wrong,
but killing is fine.

00:25:22.479 --> 00:25:29.210
The books often explore how knighthood and
honour culture empower bad men to hurt innocent

00:25:29.210 --> 00:25:30.470
people.

00:25:30.470 --> 00:25:35.950
In the books, Criston kills Joffrey not at
a wedding, but at a tournament while fighting

00:25:35.950 --> 00:25:40.039
in a melee – which is a less terrible crime.

00:25:40.039 --> 00:25:43.990
Deaths do happen at tournaments – like those
knights in Episode 1.

00:25:43.990 --> 00:25:49.489
But beating a man to death at a royal wedding,
and punching the future king consort in the

00:25:49.489 --> 00:25:52.049
face, are very serious crimes.

00:25:52.049 --> 00:25:57.700
But somehow Criston escapes the wedding and
goes to the godswood.

00:25:57.700 --> 00:26:04.440
He can’t imagine any honourable life for
himself, so he prepares to commit suicide.

00:26:04.440 --> 00:26:07.770
But he’s stopped by Alicent.

00:26:07.770 --> 00:26:09.590
Alicent needs allies.

00:26:09.590 --> 00:26:11.419
Criston needs purpose.

00:26:11.419 --> 00:26:13.840
And both these guys are angry at Rhaenyra.

00:26:13.840 --> 00:26:19.159
So maybe they’ll make an alliance, and Queen
Alicent might protect Criston from punishment

00:26:19.159 --> 00:26:20.159
for his murder.

00:26:20.159 --> 00:26:24.929
After the Joffrey’s death, the planned celebrations
are cancelled.

00:26:24.929 --> 00:26:30.610
Rhaenyra and Laenor are hastily married, as
Laenor sobs for his dead lover.

00:26:30.610 --> 00:26:37.320
In the books, Joffrey is comatose for six
days, and Laenor stays by his side until Joffrey

00:26:37.320 --> 00:26:38.320
dies.

00:26:38.320 --> 00:26:44.359
King Viserys collapses again, and his crown
falls off his head – highlighting that Viserys

00:26:44.359 --> 00:26:49.529
may die soon, and that the succession for
his crown is uncertain.

00:26:49.529 --> 00:26:55.559
A rat nibbles at Joffrey’s blood, which
could represent Larys, whose words to Alicent

00:26:55.559 --> 00:26:57.149
fed this conflict.

00:26:57.149 --> 00:27:02.879
The rat could also represent all the lords
and knights who are eager to fight for power

00:27:02.879 --> 00:27:08.109
– like crows feasting on the corpse of House
Targaryen.

00:27:08.109 --> 00:27:13.609
Everyone feels that war is coming, and they
can almost taste the blood.

00:27:13.609 --> 00:27:18.450
If you want to know more about the magic of
the old gods, about Bran and Bloodraven, and

00:27:18.450 --> 00:27:23.090
Arya skinchanging a cat – you’ve gotta
check out the Game of Thrones books.

00:27:23.090 --> 00:27:25.820
The main series has Bran and Arya’s magic.

00:27:25.820 --> 00:27:30.889
A Knight of the Seven Kingdoms features Bloodraven’s
past life as a spymaster.

00:27:30.889 --> 00:27:36.710
The World of Ice and Fire is full of worldbuilding
and a short summary of House of the Dragon.

00:27:36.710 --> 00:27:42.649
And Fire &amp; Blood tells the full story of Hot
D. You can get any one of these on audiobook

00:27:42.649 --> 00:27:44.759
for free right now at audible.com/asx.

